From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 15:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] carry errors only in the driver's own log

A healthy boot wrote 91 driver lines, halPollDbgCr alone fourteen
identical ones. Default every module to the error class; the dbgLevel proc
entry raises any of them at runtime. Two messages that are not errors stop
claiming to be: the world-wide regulatory fallback, and a regulatory state
transition the driver recovers from, which also loses its assert.

Measured: 6 driver lines a boot, and no backtrace.

Signed-off-by: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
---
--- a/wlan/mgmt/rlm_domain.c
+++ b/wlan/mgmt/rlm_domain.c
@@ -3068,7 +3068,7 @@ const struct ieee80211_regdomain *rlmDomainSearchRegdomainFromLocalDataBase(char
 		idx++;
 	}
 
-	DBGLOG(RLM, ERROR, "%s(): Error, Cannot find the correct RegDomain. country = %s.\n",
+	DBGLOG(RLM, WARN, "%s(): no local RegDomain for %s, using world-wide\n",
 			__func__, alpha2);
 	DBGLOG(RLM, INFO, "    Set as default WW.\n");
 
--- a/wlan/os/linux/gl_cfg80211.c
+++ b/wlan/os/linux/gl_cfg80211.c
@@ -3429,9 +3429,7 @@ mtk_reg_notify(IN struct wiphy *pWiphy,
 			/* Change to same state or same country, ignore */
 			return;
 	} else if (rlmDomainIsCtrlStateEqualTo(REGD_STATE_INVALID)) {
-		DBGLOG(RLM, ERROR, "\n%s():\n---> WARNING. Transit to invalid state.\n", __func__);
-		DBGLOG(RLM, ERROR, "---> WARNING.\n ");
-		rlmDomainAssert(0);
+		DBGLOG(RLM, WARN, "%s(): transit to invalid state\n", __func__);
 #if 0
 		return; /*error state*/
 #endif
--- a/wlan/os/linux/gl_init.c
+++ b/wlan/os/linux/gl_init.c
@@ -1097,16 +1097,14 @@ VOID wlanDebugInit(VOID)
 		aucDebugModule[i] = CFG_DEFAULT_DBG_LEVEL;
 #else
 
-	for (i = 0; i < DBG_MODULE_NUM; i++) {
-		aucDebugModule[i] = DBG_CLASS_ERROR |
-			DBG_CLASS_WARN | DBG_CLASS_STATE | DBG_CLASS_EVENT;// | DBG_CLASS_INFO;
-	}
-	aucDebugModule[DBG_TX_IDX] &= ~(DBG_CLASS_EVENT | DBG_CLASS_INFO);
-	aucDebugModule[DBG_RX_IDX] &= ~(DBG_CLASS_EVENT | DBG_CLASS_INFO);
-	aucDebugModule[DBG_REQ_IDX] &= ~(DBG_CLASS_EVENT | DBG_CLASS_INFO);
+	/* The state and event classes narrate a working boot, and this driver's
+	 * warnings repeat once per poll, so a healthy card fills the log. Carry
+	 * errors only; the dbgLevel proc entry raises any module at runtime.
+	 */
+	for (i = 0; i < DBG_MODULE_NUM; i++)
+		aucDebugModule[i] = DBG_CLASS_ERROR;
+
 	aucDebugModule[DBG_INTR_IDX] = 0;
-	aucDebugModule[DBG_MEM_IDX] = DBG_CLASS_ERROR | DBG_CLASS_WARN;
-	aucDebugModule[DBG_REQ_IDX] = DBG_CLASS_MASK;
 
 #endif
 #endif /* DBG */
